  SCENARIO
  =================
  Continuation of the TAN AH BENG cardiology scenario.

  Timeline so far:
    2026-05-12  Initial visit. Dr Ruth Kam diagnoses AF + HTN.
                Prescribes XARELTO 20 mg + CONCOR 5 mg + COVERSYL 5 mg.
                Initial 30-day dispense same day.
    2026-06-11  Refill of all three at clinic dispensary.
    2026-07-11  Another refill of all three (not shown).
    2026-08-12  THIS VISIT — 3-month follow-up consultation with Dr Kam.

  What happens at the 2026-08-12 visit:
    1. Dr Kam reviews the patient's medications, BP log, and recent labs.
    2. Patient is doing well on XARELTO + CONCOR + COVERSYL.
    3. Recent LDL came back at 4.1 mmol/L — above target for AF + HTN patient.
       Dr Kam ADDS CRESTOR 10 mg OD for lipid control.
    4. Patient mentions taking Vitamin D3 2,000 IU daily, bought OTC, for the
       past 4 months. Dr Kam records it on the list (NOT in SDD — Non-SDD
       fallback, code NONHSAMANAGED).
    5. Dr Kam updates the GCMS medication list — this RECONCILED VIEW
       is what putPatientMedicationList submits to NEHR.

  Resulting PML contains 5 entries:
    1. XARELTO 20 mg OD       (active, since 2026-05-12)        — SDD
    2. CONCOR 5 mg OD         (active, since 2026-05-12)        — SDD
    3. COVERSYL 5 mg OD       (active, since 2026-05-12)        — SDD
    4. CRESTOR 10 mg OD       (newly added 2026-08-12)          — SDD
    5. Vitamin D3 2,000 IU OD (active OTC, patient self-source) — Non-SDD

  KEY DIFFERENCES vs putOrderedMedications / putDispensedMedications
  =================
  putPatientMedicationList uses a FHIR-influenced structure:
    list > entry > item > MedicationStatement

  Each entry's MedicationStatement carries:
    - medicationReference (the SDD/Non-SDD code triple)
    - dosage (route + timing + quantityRange)
    - status (active / on-hold / stopped / completed)
    - dateAsserted (when the clinician confirmed this med)
    - reasonForUseCodeableConcept (clinical reason)
    - informationSource (where the info was reconciled from)
    - supportingInformation > medicationOrder/medicationDispense
        (links back to the originating order(s) and dispense(s) — these
         reference IDs are pivotal for NEHR reconciliation)

  And the list itself carries:
    - reviewedUpon (review trigger code)
    - sourceOfMedicationList (computer record / patient / family / etc.)
    - medicalAlert, drugAllergy, notesforHCP — clinical context for readers

  ANNOTATION FORMAT
  =================
    [M | O | C]   Significance: Mandatory / Optional / Conditional Mandatory
    card N        Cardinality
    Data type / length

  CODESET NOTES
  =================
  SDD entries use Singapore Drug Dictionary as codingSchemeName.
  The Vitamin D3 entry uses Non_Singapore_Drug_Dictionary_(NEHR) with the
  fallback code NONHSAMANAGED — this is the NEHR-managed catch-all for
  OTC items / supplements / drugs not in the SDD prescribing subset.

  SMST OPT-OUT
  =================
  Same as the other medication interfaces — SMST coded triples are shown
  populated with [SMST] markers; omit the coded sub-elements and retain
  textDescription if the opt-out stands.
================================================================================
